<title>MEXICO: GCC sees Q4 1996 margins up.</title>
<headline>GCC sees Q4 1996 margins up.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cement firm Grupo Cementos de Chihuahua (GCC) expected its 1996 fourth quarter operating margins to rise from the previous quarter, a company spokesman told Reuters on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;There is excess capacity, but margins were up from the third quarter so to the extent our utilisation increases, there is scope for increasing margins,&quot; said Jaime Fernandez, GCC's director of finance and planning.</p>
<p>GCC posted an operating margin of 26.6 percent for the third quarter of 1996, down from 27.7 percent.</p>
<p>((--Daniel Perez, Monterrey bureau +528 345-7617))</p>
